# Environment File Protection Rule

## Rule
Never modify environment files or run commands that overwrite them. API keys live only in `.env.local`.

## Forbidden Actions (NEVER)

- Never modify `.env.local`, `.env`, or any environment file
- Never set system environment variables
- Never run `vercel env pull` (overwrites .env.local)
- Never paste API keys in chat windows — they are auto-revoked when exposed

## Allowed Actions

- Read env vars via `process.env` in code
- Document required vars in `.env.example`
- Run `npm run check:apis` to verify keys (reads .env.local via dotenv)

## Key Management

1. Rotate keys in the provider console (Anthropic, Deepgram, etc.)
2. Paste new keys only into `.env.local` via a text editor
3. Verify with `npm run check:apis`
4. Restart dev server after changes

## This Rule Is Mandatory

Applies to all AI agents (Cursor, Codex, etc.) and human contributors.
